---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const shots = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9].map((n) => `/images/000${n}.jpg`);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Pebble 2 Button Fix"
  description="In-depth Pebble 2 side-button repair using 3D-printed moulds and Sugru — by Cedric A. Solidon."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legacy guide</p>
      <h1>Pebble 2 button fix</h1>
      <p>by Cedric A. Solidon — buttons wear out; moulded Sugru replacements hold up longer (though firmer).</p>
      <p class="muted"><strong>Note:</strong> This procedure usually ends water resistance. Proceed with eyes open.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:820px">
      <div class="panel" style="padding:1.4rem; margin-bottom:1rem">
        <h3><span class="mono" style="color:var(--orange)">1.</span> Get the 3D plan</h3>
        <p class="muted" style="margin:0">
          Search Thingiverse for <strong>pebble2 side cover by Yusukeyusuke</strong> and download the mould files.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel" style="padding:1.4rem; margin-bottom:1rem">
        <h3><span class="mono" style="color:var(--orange)">2.</span> Print your mould</h3>
        <p class="muted" style="margin:0">
          ABS works well. Chase detail — soft mushy prints make soft mushy buttons. 3D Hubs / local printers are fine if you lack a machine.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel" style="padding:1.4rem; margin-bottom:1rem">
        <h3><span class="mono" style="color:var(--orange)">3.</span> Form the buttons</h3>
        <p class="muted" style="margin:0">
          Two packs of Sugru: one for the button blank, one to bond it. 24h cure. Use a release agent (cling film, petroleum jelly, or baking spray) so Sugru leaves the mould cleanly.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel" style="padding:1.4rem; margin-bottom:2rem">
        <h3><span class="mono" style="color:var(--orange)">4.</span> Attach</h3>
        <p class="muted" style="margin:0">
          Thin Sugru on the case corners, seat the new button, clean squeeze-out, wait the full cure. Test clicks before you call it done.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid-2">
        {shots.map((src, i) => (
          <figure style="margin:0">
            <img src={src} alt={`Button fix step ${i + 1}`} loading="lazy" style="border-radius:14px; border:1px solid var(--line)" />
          </figure>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:2rem">
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/repair">← Back to repair hub</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
